# Cloudflare Pages response headers
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/platform/headers/
#
# NOTE: _headers matches on path only — it cannot target *.pages.dev
# specifically, and Cloudflare applies this file to EVERY deployment of the
# project (including a custom domain attached later). While the production
# domain is still TBD the whole site only exists on *.pages.dev, so a blanket
# noindex is the correct, safe behaviour right now.
#
# Before attaching a production custom domain you must do one of:
#   1. remove the `X-Robots-Tag: noindex` line below, or
#   2. add a Cloudflare Transform Rule on the custom hostname that removes
#      the X-Robots-Tag response header.
# Leaving it in place would keep the live site out of search engines.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  # Explicitly allow the microphone (needed by the meter) and block the rest.
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(self)

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
